  "awb---faq-data": "<div data-rt-embed-type='true'><div data-rt-embed-type='true'><script> window.awbFAQ = {\"heading\": \"Driver Application Questions, Answered\", \"items\": [{\"q\": \"What is a driver application form?\", \"a\": \"It is the application a carrier collects before someone drives for it. For drivers of commercial motor vehicles, 49 CFR 391.21 sets the minimum contents, from license details to a signed statement that the answers are true.\"}, {\"q\": \"How do I build a driver application form template?\", \"a\": \"Describe your fleet and the licenses you hire for to Emergent's <a href='https://emergent.sh/ai-form-builder'>AI form builder</a>. It builds a driver application form template with screening rules and an applicant database, and you change any question by prompting.\"}, {\"q\": \"Does the federal government publish a driver application form template?\", \"a\": \"Yes, as a sample. FMCSA posts a free driver employment application that follows the federal list in 49 CFR 391.21. Carriers may use any layout instead. Whatever template you pick, confirm it asks for employers from the past 3 years plus every commercial driving job in the 7 years before them.\"}, {\"q\": \"Is a paper driver application form enough?\", \"a\": \"For the rule itself, yes. A paper or PDF driver application form satisfies 49 CFR 391.21 once it is complete and signed. The trouble comes later: nobody hears that an applicant lacks an endorsement, and MVR orders end up in a separate spreadsheet. An app Emergent builds can alert the recruiter when an application arrives without the endorsement the job needs.\"}, {\"q\": \"Is a driver application form used for non-CDL drivers too?\", \"a\": \"Often, yes. FMCSA's driver rules begin at 10,001 pounds for vehicles in interstate commerce, while a CDL begins at 26,001 pounds. Someone driving a 16,000-pound straight truck between states needs the full application and no CDL.\"}, {\"q\": \"Which license fields does a commercial driver application form include?\", \"a\": \"Each license held, with its number and the state that issued it, plus the expiration date. Most carriers also ask for the class and endorsements, because the freight decides whether a driver needs H for hazmat or N for tankers.\"}, {\"q\": \"What questions go on a blank driver application form?\", \"a\": \"The federal list sets the sections. Identity details and 3 years of addresses come first. Work history and the crash and ticket record for the last 3 years take the most room. One box asks whether any license was ever denied, suspended, or revoked.\"}, {\"q\": \"What does a driver application form include that a job application does not?\", \"a\": \"The driving record. A driver application form adds each license and its expiration date, the accidents and violations of the past 3 years, and commercial driving jobs going back 10 years. Office and warehouse roles use a standard <a href='https://emergent.sh/ai-form-builder/job-application-form'>job application form</a> instead.\"}, {\"q\": \"Can applicants fill out a driver application form online?\", \"a\": \"Yes. Under 49 CFR 390.32, records a carrier must keep may be electronic, and an applicant may sign electronically. Emergent can build the form with e-signature capture and save each signed copy to a database you own. Within 30 days the carrier still needs driving records and previous-employer answers, often requested with a background check form.\"}, {\"q\": \"Does a driver application form include drug and alcohol history?\", \"a\": \"Indirectly. Previous-employer inquiries cover DOT drug and alcohol violations, and FMCSA-regulated carriers run that check through the Drug and Alcohol Clearinghouse. The driver approves the query inside the Clearinghouse, apart from any drug test consent form.\"}]}; </script></div></div>"
 }
}